# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JClaw - Play Framework 1.x .gitignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.mcp.json

# JCLAW-213 throwaway PoC (standalone DJL+ONNX image-caption spike + ~245MB downloaded
# model weights). Never committed; the production captioner lives in app/services/caption.
/spike/

# VulnHunter security-audit output (the /vulnhunt skill writes to
# <basename>_VULNHUNT_RESULTS_<timestamp>/). NEVER commit — these trees hold
# working exploit PoCs + step-by-step reproduction for findings that are not yet
# fixed; publishing them is an attacker roadmap. Actionable content is tracked in
# JIRA (e.g. epic JCLAW-776); keep the raw artifacts local only.
*_VULNHUNT_RESULTS_*/

# Per-clone runtime security material — application secret (PLAY_SECRET)
# and TLS cert+key. Lives under certs/ (write paths: `./jclaw.sh secret`,
# `./jclaw.sh cert`, `play secret`, `play enable-https`, the Docker
# entrypoint). NEVER commit — the secret is an admin-session-forgery
# primitive and the TLS private key binds to a per-machine CA root.
# certs/.env.example is the tracked template that keeps the directory
# in the repo and dist tarball; everything else under certs/ is
# generated and per-machine.
certs/*
!certs/.env.example

# Environment files (don't commit secrets!)
# All environment overrides live in conf/application.conf with %prod. / %test.
# prefixes — there are no per-environment conf files. Only secrets are
# gitignored, via .env (loaded by jclaw.sh into the JVM environment).
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Play Framework runtime files
tmp/
logs/
*.log
*.pid

# Play precompiled files
precompiled/

# `play javadoc` output
javadoc/

# Benchmark/harness run output. Same rule as evals/reports/ below: a report is a
# measurement of one run on one machine, not a fact about the code, so it ages
# into noise and bloats the history. Keep a baseline you want to diff against out
# of band.
reports/

# Eval run output (JCLAW-875). The suites in evals/suites/ ARE tracked — they
# are the measuring stick. Reports are per-run measurements: keep the ones you
# want to compare against out of band, not in the history.
evals/reports/

# Memory-quality eval suites (JCLAW-529). Unlike evals/suites/, these are
# GENERATED FROM THE OPERATOR'S OWN MEMORY CORPUS, so a case's query and its gold
# answers are personal data by construction — "what is my NAS IP" is the secret,
# not just a pointer to it. This repository is mirrored publicly, so they must
# never be tracked. MemoryEvalPaths refuses to write outside this directory
# rather than relying on the ignore rule alone.
evals/local/

# Claude Code and OpenAI Codex config.
# Note: `.claude/*` (contents) instead of `.claude/` (directory) so git can
# still descend into .claude/ and apply the negations below — git can't
# re-include a path under a fully-ignored parent directory.
.claude/*
.agents/

# …but keep checked-in slash commands so they survive fresh clones.
# Other .claude/ subdirs (settings.local.json, state, etc.) stay ignored
# because they hold per-developer state that shouldn't be checked in.
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**

# Autoresearch state
.autoresearch/

# omo tool local state (per-machine, not tracked)
.omo/

# IntelliJ IDEA
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/

# VS Code (its Java language-server build output is redirected to build/ via the
# eclipse plugin in build.gradle.kts, so it no longer lands in bin/)
.vscode/

# Eclipse / Buildship IDE metadata (generated, same category as .idea/ above)
.classpath
.project
.settings/

# NetBeans
nbproject/
nbproject/private/

# Build outputs
dist/
test-result/
frontend/test-report/
*.war
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Node.js (for frontend)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/

# Frontend build outputs
frontend/.nuxt/
frontend/.output/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.cache/
public/spa/

# Operator-hosted apps (public/apps/<slug>/) are runtime data, not source.
# The app_install tool creates public/apps/ on demand and writes each app
# there. The whole directory is excluded from version control — and, since
# .distignore inherits .gitignore, from the dist bundle too — so a fresh
# checkout and the bundle have no public/apps/ until an app is installed.
/public/apps/

# SSL certificates/keys (defense-in-depth wildcards — the certs/ directory
# itself is handled above with a !certs/.gitkeep negation). `.cert` is
# jclaw's chosen extension via `./jclaw.sh cert` and `play enable-https`;
# `.crt` is the more common convention elsewhere — we list both.
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cert
*.p12
*.jks

# lib/ — was the 1.12 dep target (populated by `play deps --sync`); in 1.13.x
# (PF-90) Gradle resolves deps into ~/.gradle/caches/ and never writes to lib/.
# Directory may still exist as stale leftover from a previous 1.12 build; in
# either case never tracked.
lib/

# Database files
data/
*.db
*.h2.db
*.mv.db
*.sql
# conf/db/*.sql holds checked-in schema scripts (e.g. db-scheduler's
# scheduled_tasks DDL) that ship with the app. The global *.sql ignore
# above is for transient H2 dumps and similar generated files.
!conf/db/*.sql
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Test coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/
jacoco.exec
jacoco.xml

# Code quality scanners — sonar-scanner CLI (and the SonarQube MCP that
# wraps it) creates this on every analysis run to hold caches, the local
# report, and scan metadata. Never tracked.
.scannerwork/

# Play modules — populated by Gradle's `extractPlayModules` task at build
# time (copies framework-bundled modules from frameworkPath/modules/<name>
# to <app>/modules/<name>). Regenerated each build, never tracked.
modules/*

# BMAD method install state and output (regenerated by ./jclaw.sh setup
# via `npx bmad-method install`). The install creates ~270 files under
# _bmad/ and ~42 skills under .claude/skills/. Both directories are
# gitignored so BMAD upgrades — which delete and rewrite hundreds of
# files between minor versions (e.g. 6.2.2 → 6.5.0 moved skill manifests
# from _bmad/<module>/<skill>/SKILL.md to .claude/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md)
# — produce zero git diffs. The setup script re-runs the install on
# every fresh clone, restoring slash commands without committed churn.
#
# _bmad/custom/config.toml is the one exception, and it is deliberate: BMAD
# never writes it (the installer regenerates _bmad/config.toml and
# _bmad/bmm/config.yaml around it), and it is the only durable place to pin a
# project-level value. Without it tracked, every clone silently reverts to the
# installed defaults — e.g. project_knowledge points at docs/ root, so the next
# /bmad-document-project writes a competing doc set beside docs/architecture/
# instead of updating it. BMAD ships _bmad/custom/.gitignore (`*.user.toml`)
# expecting that directory to be tracked; a blanket `_bmad/` rule makes that
# file inert, because git never descends into an excluded directory.
#
# Each level must be re-included explicitly for the same reason — a bare
# `!_bmad/custom/config.toml` under `_bmad/` is a silent no-op.
_bmad/*
!_bmad/custom/
_bmad/custom/*
!_bmad/custom/config.toml
_bmad-output/

# Global skills (track all skills in the registry)
# Agent workspace copies are excluded via the workspace/* rule below.
#
# Skill-bundled binaries are excluded: they're platform-specific, typically
# large (~tens of MB), and should be fetched by the skill's install step
# rather than tracked in git. SKILL.md stays; the binary under tools/ does not.
skills/whatsapp-wacli-mac/tools/wacli

# Python bytecode from skill scripts (regenerated on every run, never tracked)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Note: per-skill `credentials/` directories ARE tracked here, but only as
# README templates that document the expected JSON shape. Real secret files
# (radarr.json, etc.) live operator-local in workspace/main/skills/<skill>/
# credentials/, which is gitignored via the workspace/* rule below.

# Agent workspaces — never tracked (JCLAW-910). Everything under here is operator
# state: SOUL/IDENTITY/USER/BOOTSTRAP/AGENT are edited by the operator and written
# to by agents at runtime. The default agent's SOUL and IDENTITY ship as templates
# in WorkspaceFiles and are scaffolded at boot by DefaultConfigJob, so a fresh
# install still gets them without the files living in git.
#
# main's five markdown files used to be tracked via `!` exceptions here. That made
# every release sweep the operator's own edits into a public commit — USER.md in
# particular carried their name, employer and location.
workspace/

# Test workspaces (ephemeral, created by integration tests)
workspace-test/

# Ignore but keep empty directories
!.gitkeep

# Backup files
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp

# Maven/Gradle local
.mvn/
.gradle/
build/

# PlayWright files
.playwright-mcp/

# graphify knowledge graph — rebuilt locally from source, per-machine
graphify-out/

# Tranco seed list for the scrape corpus builder (JCLAW-1081) — ~22 MB, regenerable
evals/scrape/.cache/

# Generated by `jclaw.sh shim` on Windows (JCLAW-1105); never committed.
/jclaw.cmd
